It uses or adapts software and models developed by third parties:

NAVSIM devkit v1.1, Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/autonomousvision/navsim
  superglance/executor/pdm.py scores candidate trajectories with NAVSIM's PDM simulator and PDM scorer and repeats
  the ego-progress normalization of navsim/evaluate/pdm_score.py; superglance/executor/sidecar.py and stitched.py run
  the PDM simulator. NAVSIM itself is imported, not included.

nuPlan-devkit, Copyright 2021 Motional, Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/motional/nuplan-devkit
  Imported by the executor (ego state and vehicle parameters); not included.

Qwen3.5-9B, Apache License 2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B
  The base vision-language model. Its weights are not included; the trainers load it through transformers.

Qwen-2.5-1B-RLCD, core/engine_torch.py, Apache License 2.0 (repository metadata).
  https://huggingface.co/harshatheg/Qwen-2.5-1B-RLCD
  The option-letter readout of superglance/model/prompt.py (one sequence per question with all its options, the
  candidate logits at the answer position) follows it.

AlpaSim, Apache License 2.0.
  The closed-loop simulator of the paper. superglance/alpasim/driver.py serves AlpaSim's egodriver gRPC interface
  (AlpaSim's alpasim_grpc package, imported, not included), superglance/alpasim/collisions.py reads its rollout logs
  with its alpasim_utils package, and superglance/eval/pai_inputs.py re-projects f-theta frames with the camera model of
  AlpaSim's rectification.py. AlpaSim itself is not included.

Waymo Open Dataset, rater_feedback_utils.py, Copyright 2025 The Waymo Open Dataset Authors, Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/waymo-research/waymo-open-dataset
  superglance/builders/pools/rater_feedback_utils.py is that file, unchanged: the WOD-E2E rater feedback score.

Language2Drive SDK and benchmark scorer.
  superglance/l2d/adapter.py implements the SDK's model-adapter interface, scripts/l2d_run.sh runs the SDK and
  scripts/eval_l2d.sh its scorer, and superglance/builders/instructions/ imports its trajectory verifier. The SDK and the
  scorer are not included.

Qwen-Drive-1.0.
  scripts/eval_pai_qwen_drive.sh runs its released planning script on our PAI-AV frames, and superglance/eval/qd_pai_scenes.py
  and qd_pai_score.py import its code to write its scene format and to score its plans. Its code and weights are not included.

PhysicalAI-AV devkit (physical_ai_av).
  Imported by superglance/builders/shards/pai_inputs.py and superglance/eval/qd_pai_scenes.py to read the dataset; not
  included.
